    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nOption validators and setters repeatedly pass error buffers and their sizes separately. Some setters return messages in static storage.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\n- Introduce `CharBuf` for borrowed writable storage and its byte count, including space for a terminating NUL.\r\n- Move option error buffers to callers, preserving sizes, truncation, and calls that do not need a message.\r\n- Consolidate option error formatting and allowed-value lists.\r\n- Return errors directly from `do_one_set_option()`.\r\n- Remove unused option-setter arguments.\r\n- Fold legacy TTY compatibility handling into the existing callers.\r\n- Reuse `CharBuf` for Tree-sitter query errors.\r\n- Pass `CharBuf` through the statusline and statuscolumn builders, including title formatting.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-21T16:29:26Z",
