            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I really wanted to use String, but its `size` field describes content length, whereas the `length` field in `CharBuf` describes capacity (including space for NUL). To get the content length from a `CharBuf` we'd use `strlen()`.\r\n\r\nI avoided using `size` as that would make it extra confusing when compared to `String`. `capacity` would be more accurate but chose `length` as it seemed more keeping with the code that uses it, it's just the length of the buffer. Though happy to call it `size` if you still prefer that.\r\n\r\nI'll add a comment to attempt to make this a bit clearer.",
            "commit_id": "04472c48b29b323b9453f51ad7c974c452ecce12",
            "created_at": "2026-09-21T13:49:50Z",
